  <Scene>
    <WorldInfo title="A Source Is Not a Whirlpool" info="&quot;X3D Math Lab • Static sampled geometry and authored lesson parameters; not a proof, live controller, or checkpoint.&quot;">
      <MetadataString containerField="metadata" name="mathlab.sample" reference="mathlab.x3d/1" value="&quot;{\&quot;adapter\&quot;:\&quot;mathlab.x3d/1\&quot;,\&quot;axes\&quot;:\&quot;XY plane: field positions. Cyan velocities use common scale 0.28; the integration circle stays fixed while tracers move.\&quot;,\&quot;bounds\&quot;:{\&quot;center\&quot;:[0.0,0.0,0.08],\&quot;size\&quot;:[5.94,5.94,0.74]},\&quot;configuration_sha256\&quot;:\&quot;dff3d499b9553f4680bd7696e028c01842b2ab7b0cd0f6ae4b76410e7a2812de\&quot;,\&quot;insights\&quot;:[\&quot;Cyan velocity arrows use one common display scale 0.28; they are not normalized independently. Their lengths remain comparable.\&quot;,\&quot;The amber disk boundary is fixed at radius R. The mint ring is a separate set of moving fluid tracers. Flux/circulation refer to amber; area growth refers to mint.\&quot;,\&quot;This field has exact flow X(t)=exp(at)R(bt)X(0), so the tracer picture has no numerical ODE-step error. Counterclockwise b&gt;0 is positive rotation.\&quot;,\&quot;The 128-point parametric boundary sums independently check the analytic flux and circulation. Constant integrands make this an especially clean Green's-theorem example, not a test of quadrature accuracy on arbitrary fields.\&quot;,\&quot;Changing R changes total flux and circulation in proportion to area; the local divergence and curl stay fixed. One rotating marker reveals motion a perfectly unmarked circle would hide.\&quot;],\&quot;lesson\&quot;:\&quot;vector_field\&quot;,\&quot;metrics\&quot;:[{\&quot;id\&quot;:\&quot;divergence\&quot;,\&quot;label\&quot;:\&quot;Divergence\&quot;,\&quot;note\&quot;:\&quot;Instantaneous fractional area-growth rate for this velocity field.\&quot;,\&quot;unit\&quot;:\&quot;\&quot;,\&quot;value\&quot;:0.4},{\&quot;id\&quot;:\&quot;curl\&quot;,\&quot;label\&quot;:\&quot;Out-of-plane curl\&quot;,\&quot;note\&quot;:\&quot;Counterclockwise is positive. Rigid-body angular speed is b, half this curl.\&quot;,\&quot;unit\&quot;:\&quot;\&quot;,\&quot;value\&quot;:1.6},{\&quot;id\&quot;:\&quot;flux\&quot;,\&quot;label\&quot;:\&quot;Outward flux: fixed circle\&quot;,\&quot;note\&quot;:\&quot;\&quot;,\&quot;unit\&quot;:\&quot;\&quot;,\&quot;value\&quot;:2.1237166338267004},{\&quot;id\&quot;:\&quot;circulation\&quot;,\&quot;label\&quot;:\&quot;CCW circulation: fixed circle\&quot;,\&quot;note\&quot;:\&quot;\&quot;,\&quot;unit\&quot;:\&quot;\&quot;,\&quot;value\&quot;:8.494866535306802},{\&quot;id\&quot;:\&quot;area\&quot;,\&quot;label\&quot;:\&quot;Tracer area ÷ initial area\&quot;,\&quot;note\&quot;:\&quot;Exact flow determinant exp(2at); the integration circle remains fixed.\&quot;,\&quot;unit\&quot;:\&quot;×\&quot;,\&quot;value\&quot;:1.3771277643359572}],\&quot;parameters\&quot;:{\&quot;a\&quot;:0.2,\&quot;b\&quot;:0.8,\&quot;radius\&quot;:1.3,\&quot;time\&quot;:0.8},\&quot;sample_schema\&quot;:\&quot;mathlab.sample/1\&quot;,\&quot;sample_sha256\&quot;:\&quot;7d819790ada24ca0df433d329ce865b487da11aafcd761a009de503eed8d0e4e\&quot;,\&quot;scope\&quot;:\&quot;Static sampled geometry and authored lesson parameters; not a proof, live controller, or checkpoint.\&quot;,\&quot;title\&quot;:\&quot;A Source Is Not a Whirlpool\&quot;,\&quot;view\&quot;:\&quot;planar\&quot;}&quot;" />
    </WorldInfo>
